Drop sis from the riscv toolchain build set.

sis is the RTEMS instruction simulator.  Nothing in this project runs it:
every lane runs under QEMU, and the image exists to provide a compiler, a
BSP and QEMU.  Upstream RSB appends it to 7/rtems-riscv.bset as the last
package in the set, so it contributes nothing to the toolchain and fails
at the very end of a seventy-minute build.

It has failed three consecutive CI builds and blocks every other job,
because both lanes pull an image that is never published.  What is known:

  * The source downloads correctly -- 303.5 kB, complete -- from
    gitlab.rtems.org after the dl.rtems.org content cache 404s, which it
    does for several other packages in the same run without harm.  The
    first diagnosis, that this was a transient outage, was wrong.
  * The build then fails about four seconds in.  The RSB error report
    ends part way through the %build trace, right after the setup step's
    "rm -rf rtems-sis-<hash>", so the failure is in unpacking or
    configuring rather than anywhere deep.
  * The RSB says as much itself: "In some cases the error appears only in
    the complete build log".  That log is inside the build container and
    is discarded with it.

So this is a stopgap, not a diagnosis, and it is headed as one.  Why sis
does not build on Ubuntu 24.04 is worth answering -- it is upstream's
build set, and anyone building a riscv toolchain from this pin hits it --
but not at seventy minutes per iteration while it blocks everything else.

Drop this patch once that is understood.  See rtems-esphome#76.

diff --git a/rtems/config/7/rtems-riscv.bset b/rtems/config/7/rtems-riscv.bset
index 3b76448..41b69a4 100644
--- a/rtems/config/7/rtems-riscv.bset
+++ b/rtems/config/7/rtems-riscv.bset
@@ -3,4 +3,3 @@
 %define with_libgomp
 %define with_newlib_tls
 %include 7/rtems-default
-devel/sis-2-1
